    "tempo": 100,
    "notes": "Classic 4-minute pop song, a little prog / a little yacht rock -- Supertramp lane (Logical Song / Take the Long Way Home territory: quartal-adjacent extended chords at density='full', laid-back light-swing pocket, sax-like countermelody). Structure: intro, verse, chorus, verse, chorus, transition (real breakdown -- learned from Cakewalk Strut not to stay 'too alive' the whole way through), bridge (borrowed bVII for a modal-mixture lift + second_melody carrying a genuine polymeter drift as the 'prog' touch), final chorus modulated up a whole step G->A (uses the sec_key/sec_mode fix made today -- confirmed counterpoint and second_melody now actually follow a section-level key override instead of silently staying in the piece's original key), outro. swing=0.15 throughout on purpose (unlike the cakewalk/ragtime rule of swing=0.0 -- yacht rock's pocket, e.g. Steely Dan/Doobie Brothers, genuinely does want a light shuffle, a different genre calling for a different informed choice, not the same rule applied blindly). Counterpoint (one voice, below, sax/horn-like) present only in choruses/bridge/final chorus, absent in verses -- enters with the hook the way Xanadu's counterpoint did.",
